From ed783fc102c63af854c26e17c64e81fbd52823a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: devmilan <devmilan@noreply.codeberg.org>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 23:23:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] checkpoint: import an NVFP4 release as its codes beside the
 e4m3 table over the tensor's f32 global, and per-channel FP8 by its row scale

The checkpoint's global is the DIVISOR its quantiser scaled the weights by, which a
dequant applies in reverse -- the reciprocal vLLM's own scheme and the TensorRT-LLM
runner form at load -- so the scale a piece reads is the e4m3 table divided by it,
owned, one a 16 of K. A tensor without its weight_packed/weight_scale/
weight_global_scale trio is not NVFP4 and takes the stock path, so a release mixing
NVFP4 MLPs with per-channel FP8 or bf16 linears reads every weight by its own form;
a missing or zero global is refused by name at the weight.

FP8's scale plane is looked up by both spellings, X.weight_scale_inv and X.weight_scale:
a [N, 1] one is per-channel fp8, never trivial (no kernel serves the form) but read
by the row's scale, and stated as [1, K] so the value reads piece by piece. A weight
whose scale is of a shape no encoding states gets no encoding, and the read refuses
it with the reason rather than index a [N, 1] plane as a [N, K/128] one.

data/recipes/q38-27b-nvfp4-df2.recipe: unsloth's NVFP4 Qwen3.8-27B with the DFlash2
drafter -- the trunk at OCP-MXFP4, the head at block fp8, the drafter as small as
its acceptance allows. The README and the GUIDE name it beside its rad-convert
command; the recipe test holds its patterns to the declared names of the model it
was written for.
